# Named bounded unit handlers keep their effect row and failure type as
# function values. A parameter of the same type accepts them, the row and the
# failure travel with the value, and a named handler crosses into a task,
# with the same output at O0, O1 and O2. Mismatched contracts are still
# refused: a wider row (E0747), a failure where the parameter says `Never`
# (E0112), and a `&` parameter where the function type reads (E0227).
fixture: named_handler_keeps_its_contract_as_a_value.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet check allowed.jet
exit: 0
step: jet run -O0 allowed.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "tick 1\ntick 2\nok 3\nrejected -4\ntick 5\ndone\n"
step: jet run -O1 allowed.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "tick 1\ntick 2\nok 3\nrejected -4\ntick 5\ndone\n"
step: jet run -O2 allowed.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "tick 1\ntick 2\nok 3\nrejected -4\ntick 5\ndone\n"
step: jet check wider_row.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "Error [jet.CallbackEffectBoundExceeded]: This callback uses the effect `IO`, which the parameter doesn't allow\n  --> wider_row.jet:14:17" # the row travels with the value
step: jet check failure.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "Error [jet.ValueTypeMismatch]: `accept_total` wants fn(Int) -[IO]> Never! for argument 1, but this is fn(Int) -[IO]> Rejected!\n  --> failure.jet:19:18" # the failure type travels with the value
step: jet check borrow.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "Error [jet.MarkedFunctionValue]: `bump` can't be used as a function value because its parameter `c` is `&`\n  --> borrow.jet:15:10" # the access mode is kept
